index 2bafc232d7..b2d64ae4a0 100644
--- a/ops/changelog.md
+++ b/ops/changelog.md
@@ -9193,3 +9193,4 @@ Did NOT modify research-roadmap.yaml or scripts/research_conductor.py. Did NOT p
 - 2026-06-16: PHASE A1 (THE HEADLINE; the deferred-from-.395 scale-up, gate now OPEN) -- DiffusionGemma energy-guided FULL benchmark with matched no-Carnot-verifier controls. The .395 capstone flipped diffusiongemma_full_run_gate=True (hardened_win=True AND exp4274 preflight_go=True). RUN the full benchmark via the llama.cpp PR binary (~/.cache/llama.cpp-master/build/bin/llama-diffusion-gemma-eval -- the ONLY working loader). Wire the verifier ensemble as a per-step GUIDANCE energy reweighting denoising token selection. On n>=30 per arm: HEADLINE/oracle-distinct arm (verifier_is_oracle=false) = a LEARNED energy verifier guiding on a REASONING domain (FoVer-step/math, where the verifier is NOT the executable oracle) vs unguided vs RFG (arXiv:2509.25604, the model's own log-likelihood-ratio self-guidance -- the NO-external-verifier control) vs EntRGi (arXiv:2602.05000); emit diffusiongemma_guidance_moat BARE bool := (Carnot-guided - RFG > 0 AND CI95-excl-0). SUPPORTING/execution-grounded arm (verifier_is_oracle=true) = an executable-oracle verifier on code/Sudoku, reported as execution_grounded (cheap/automatic/decentralized, NOT a moat). If the learned verifier cannot score partial (masked) denoising states, that is an HONEST finding (the moat arm blocks; the control comparison + execution-grounded arm still land). NO TRM training; NO leaderboard submission. (⚠️ Research Finding) — honest_verdict=complete_diffusiongemma_learned_verifier_cannot_score_partial_states; results/experiment_4281_diffusiongemma_energy_guided_full_run.json
 - 2026-06-16: PHASE B1 (HARDEN the cross-family win on a 2nd, construction-disjoint substrate) -- ARC-GEN family-disjoint cross-family stress. .395 proved cross-family generalization (exp4271 +0.4038 held-out) but on ONE substrate (the recovered 52-task manifest), inviting the 'specific to your partition' critique. ARC-GEN (arXiv:2511.00162, github.com/google/ARC-GEN) is Google's mimetic procedural generator faithfully covering ALL 400 ARC-AGI-1 + 500 ARC-AGI-2 tasks, each a parameterized generator with a NATIVE family id -- an INDEPENDENT family substrate. Clone it (GITIGNORED -- no embedded-repo gitlink), build a family-disjoint candidate pool with native family ids + exact target hashes, train the set-encoder on train-families, test beats-vote on HELD-OUT generator-families. Report cross_family_delta SEPARATELY on original-ARC / ARC-TGI / ARC-GEN families (the generators-become-their-own-distribution failure mode) + a randomized family-rich stress split (arXiv:2601.18217). Emit arcgen_cross_family_holds BARE bool := (held-out-family delta>0 AND CI95-excl-0 on the ARC-GEN families). verifier_is_oracle=false. HARD-CAP to the window; an honest partial pool (>=4 families, >=~10 held-out tasks/fold) is fine. (✅ Complete) — honest_verdict=complete: arcgen_cross_family_generalizes; results/experiment_4282_arcgen_cross_family_stress.json
 - 2026-06-16: PHASE C1 (CONTINUOUS SELF-LEARNING -- the mandated self-learning experiment) -- re-power the online verifier-weight adaptation test on the LARGER family set. research-program.md mandates >=1 self-learning experiment/milestone; Tier 1 = online weight/counter updates (CPU, <1us/update, NOT the retired live-LoRA path). .395 found static-is-the-ceiling BUT the (online-static) CI only TOUCHED 0 at n=52 ([0.0, 0.192]) -- an n-limit, not a proven null. RE-RUN the Tier-1 online reweighting across the COMBINED family set (the .395 recovered manifest + ARC-GEN's many families from exp4282, a soft input) so the CI is POWERED, AND add a Tier-2 constraint-memory arm (cache per-family selection patterns, reuse on the nearest-neighbor seen family) as a distinct mechanism. Report static vs online vs Tier-2 cross-family delta + the per-family adaptation curve + a POWERED CI95 on (online-static). Emit online_adaptation_helps BARE bool := (online-static>0 AND CI95-excl-0). A positive gain = the verifier self-improves toward generalization (north-star-grade); a null WITH POWER = static is genuinely the ceiling (retire the online-adaptation-helps ask). verifier_is_oracle=false. NO fine-tuning; NO TRM; NO live-LoRA. (✅ Complete) — honest_verdict=complete: powered_static_is_the_ceiling_for_self_learning; results/experiment_4283_self_learning_repowered_arcgen.json
+- 2026-06-16: PHASE D1 (the owed north-star §5 EFFICIENCY axis) -- energy-verifier vs LLM-as-judge head-to-head on the ORACLE-DISTINCT cross-family ARC selection. north-star §5 names the verifier's win condition: 'equally effective as the LM at lower cost/latency' (efficiency-parity), and names this head-to-head as load-bearing-owed work. On the SAME held-out-family cross-family selection task (the oracle-distinct domain -- NOT code, whose efficiency-vs-judge is retired/circular), compare the learned energy verifier's selection accuracy vs an LLM-as-judge (a cached SOTA GGUF -- Qwen3.6-35B-A3B or gemma-4 -- selecting from the same candidates). Report accuracy parity (within CI) AND the compute/latency/cost ratio (wall-clock, FLOPs-proxy, $/1k selections). Emit efficiency_parity_at_lower_cost BARE bool := (energy-verifier accuracy within the LLM-judge CI AND energy-verifier cost <= 0.1x the LLM-judge cost). Target: 'parity at 10-100x cheaper' (CompassVerifier 2508.03686 / Luna-2 small-verifier precedent: 60-1000x). verifier_is_oracle=false. This is a NEW measurement (the §5 owed axis), NOT a re-run. (✅ Complete) — honest_verdict=complete: efficiency_parity_at_lower_cost_true_delta_0.4423; results/experiment_4284_verifier_efficiency_vs_llm_judge.json
